# Always commit + push

After finishing a set of changes in this project, **always create a git commit and push to `origin`** without waiting to be asked.

## When

- After website/docs updates, itinerary data changes, scripts, rules, or collab tooling
- Do this at the end of the task once the work is complete and verified

## How

1. Follow the repo git safety protocol (`status` / `diff` / `log`, HEREDOC commit message)
2. Stage relevant files only — never secrets (`collab/google_oauth_client.json`, `collab/google_token.json`, credentials)
3. Commit with a concise why-focused message
4. `git push origin HEAD` (or the current tracking branch)
5. Briefly confirm commit + that it was pushed

## Exceptions

- If push fails (auth/network), report the error and leave the local commit in place
- Do not force-push to `main`/`master`
- Do not commit `.env` / credential files
